Article 27
(1) The Community and Business World may participate in the fulfillment of children's rights including:
a. prevention efforts;
b. risk reduction and handling of child victims of violence; c. exploitation; and
d. mistreatment and neglect, both through individual efforts and institutional efforts.
(2) The participation of the Community and Business World as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be realized through support for the fulfillment of children's rights including:
a. providing information and or reporting every situation of vulnerability and violence that comes to their knowledge;
b. facilitating or conducting prevention and risk reduction activities;
c. providing protection services for children who become victims; d. assisting advocacy for victims and/or the community regarding the handling of cases of violence, exploitation, mistreatment and neglect of children;
e. assisting the repatriation, rehabilitation and social reintegration process; f. support in the process of fulfilling other children's rights; g. establishment of integrated child service centers;
h. provision of educational scholarships;
i. provision of health cost assistance; and
j. provision of legal aid to children experiencing legal problems.
(3) The participation of the Community and Business World as referred to in paragraph (2) may be carried out by individuals, families, community organizations and companies.
(4) Further provisions regarding the procedures for participation of the Community and Business World as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be regulated in a Regent Regulation.

Article 12
Every woman has the right to:
a. live, sustain life and improve her standard of living;
b. live peacefully, safely, in peace, happily, prosperously both physically and spiritually;
c. enjoy a good and healthy living environment;
d. live in a family within the bonds of lawful marriage based on the provisions of Laws and Regulations;
e. obtain work in accordance with her abilities, appropriate conditions and fair and just wages;
f. specifically for women with disabilities, the right to obtain facilities and special treatment in public services;
g. play an active role in the field of politics and government in accordance with the potential and capabilities she possesses;
h. obtain legal information and services;
i. obtain services to increase her income; and
j. obtain other rights in accordance with her human dignity and based on the provisions of Laws and Regulations.

Article 8
Preventive efforts as referred to in Article 6 are as follows:
a. conducting legal awareness education for the community, especially for women and children;
b. developing massive and sustainable movements involving the community in prevention and handling of violence actions;
c. instilling character values, morals, and family resilience; and
d. involving the role and participation of the community in women's empowerment and child protection.

Article 13
Every child has the right to:
a. live, grow, develop and participate reasonably in accordance with human dignity and honor, and receive protection from acts of violence, exploitation, discrimination and neglect;
b. obtain their identity;
